  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in House",
    "asOf": "2025-09-03",
    "date": "2026-09-09T18:23:55Z",
    "text": "This bill directs the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) to develop guidelines to improve access to a Transportation Worker Identification Credential (TWIC) for prisoners prior to their release.\n\nSpecifically,\u00a0TSA must develop guidelines to assist individuals in federal, state, and local prisons in (1) pre-applying or preparing an application for\u00a0a TWIC card; and (2) requesting an appeal or waiver of a preliminary determination of ineligibility for a TWIC card.\n\nAs background, a TWIC card is required by the Maritime Transportation Security Act for workers who need access to secure areas of U.S. maritime facilities and vessels. TSA conducts a background check to determine a person\u2019s eligibility and issues the credential."
  },
